From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:26:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 51/72] deepseek: TF_DSV41_IDX_SPLIT cut from the rows alone,
 agreed at the TP bootstrap

The split's cut is the 64-row grid's even one of the segment's rows, so no
rank-local setting (the index budget) shapes the gather; each rank then steps
its own part in its own row blocks. The glue's checks and transfers are
idx_split.glueCut / Cut.plan, shared with the tests.

The mode is agreed through tp.Config.family instead of a boot all-gather:
off adds nothing (an off / off boot is byte-for-byte the base's), and a
refused value hashes as invalid, so a mixed pair fails the agreement on both
ranks and a refused pair fails BadKnob on both at apply.

Tests: agreement bytes, the exchange plan for every n in 256..4200, and two
ranks with unequal index budgets issuing the same collectives and owning each
row once.
